      distance" p.7.  Quoted where a limb tests a claim.
  (c) The AW+ CLI wiki -- no x960 pages exist; the x950 pages are the same generation.

Syntax, quoted verbatim from the guide, p.3:
  > awplus(config)# ip route [vrf <vrf-name>] <subnet&mask> {<gateway-ip>|<interface>}
  >                 [<distance>] [weight <1-255>] [description <description>]

**The objective this case is graded against**, since none is authored: a static route configured
on the DUT must (1) be absent by default, (2) when configured, cause frames for its prefix to be
FORWARDED to its next hop and the far end's reply to return, while a frame for a prefix with no
route is DROPPED in the same leg, (3) be removable from the FIB and not merely from
running-config, and (4) survive a reboot.  Depth beyond the floor per the Test Engineer's
2026-10-08 "satisfactory level of testing" rule: administrative distance / floating-static route
selection, the distance-255 RIB-not-FIB rule, and the interface form of the command.


