6. THE THREE FLOWS USED BY EVERY COUNTED LEG
---------------------------------------------
Sender is always 192.168.10.5 / 00:11:22:33:44:01 on eth3, next hop e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43.
A background ARP responder answers the DUT's ARP for 192.168.10.5 (`--answer`), because this DUT
does NOT learn a neighbour from a request it merely answers -- measured in group A and recorded
in `tools/README.md`.

  10.70.70.1      THE SUBJECT.  Reachable only via the static route under test (swi_b's loopback).
  10.80.80.1      THE CONTROL.  No route ever exists for it.  It must be dropped in EVERY leg,
                  including the legs where the subject is forwarded.  Sent in the SAME leg.
  192.168.10.1    THE INSTRUMENT CONTROL.  The DUT's own vlan10 address.  It must be answered in
                  EVERY leg, so that a zero on the other two is a measurement and not a dead
                  instrument.


