        x5  ICMP t0/c0 192.168.10.1  -> 192.168.10.5  [ours]        <- instrument alive
        x5  ICMP **t3/c1** 192.168.10.1 -> 192.168.10.5  [ours]

      10.70.70.1 : 5 sent, 0 echo replies, and **five ICMP type 3 CODE 1 (host unreachable)**,
      one per packet -- against type 3 **code 0** (network unreachable) in every earlier
      no-route leg.  The code change is the whole finding:

      🔎 **OBSERVATION O-2 (correct behaviour, worth recording): the interface form makes the
      prefix ON-LINK, so the DUT ARPs for the destination instead of using a next hop.**
      `is directly connected, vlan61` in the FIB means the DUT tried to resolve 10.70.70.1 by
      ARP on vlan61.  swi_b does not answer ARP for its own loopback address on that subnet, so
      resolution failed and the DUT answered **host** unreachable rather than **network**
      unreachable -- i.e. it had a route and could not reach the host, which is exactly the
      opposite failure from "no route".  The interface form is therefore for point-to-point
      links; on a VLAN/broadcast interface it is not a substitute for the next-hop form.  Not a
      defect: it matches the guide's `{<gateway-ip>|<interface>}` semantics.  The rate limit
      seen on the network-unreachable legs (2 per 10) did not apply here (5 per 5), another
      difference between the two paths.
      STEP 5 VERDICT: PASS (the form is accepted, installed and behaves as documented).

STEP 6 -- PERSISTENCE ACROSS A REBOOT.

  Nothing is written to startup-config.  A NAMED boot config is staged and the pointer put back
  afterwards (campaign rule).

  awplus(config)# no ip route 10.70.70.0/24 vlan61
  awplus(config)# ip route 10.70.70.0/24 10.0.61.2          <- back to the canonical form
  awplus# copy running-config flash:/ckT43855.cfg
  awplus# dir flash:
       2107 -rw- Oct 15 2026 07:33:35  ckT43855.cfg
  awplus# configure terminal
  awplus(config)# boot config-file flash:/ckT43855.cfg
  awplus# show boot
  Current boot config: flash:/ckT43855.cfg (file exists)
  awplus# show file flash:/ckT43855.cfg | include ip route|spanning-tree priority|vlan61
  spanning-tree priority 0
  interface vlan61
  ip route 10.70.70.0/24 10.0.61.2            <- the staged file carries the route AND the
                                                 group's STP change, so the bench returns intact

  INSTRUMENT NOTE: `copy running-config flash:/<file>` did NOT prompt (y/n) on this build when
  the destination did not already exist, so `cfg.py`'s `YN:` form timed out (exit 6) even though
  the copy itself had succeeded -- the file was on flash with the right timestamp.  `cfg.py` has
  no "may prompt" form (`YN?:` is `ckyn.py` only and is rejected by cfg.py as a command).  Use a
  plain command for this copy.
